     WO-203B: only OUR addition to the game's Libs/Config/defaultProfile.xml, inserted just before the end of its actionmap
     named "dialog" (the game's own dialogue lock: exclusive, live only while a conversation is shown) by the agent's keys-pak
     verb (dotnet/KcdMp.Client/KeybindPak.cs MergeDialog), into Mods\kdcmp\Data\kdcmp_keys.pak. The game's file is never shipped. -->
<kdcmp_patch target="Libs/Config/defaultProfile.xml" insert="end-of-actionmap:dialog">
		<!-- KCD2MP (WO-203B): leave the partner's conversation you are listening to. Its keys are the game's own Back superaction's
		     (keybindSuperactions.back.xml lists it there). Press only. -->
		<action name="kcd2mp_listen_cancel" onPress="1" keyboard="_keybinds_ref_" />
</kdcmp_patch>
